      "takeaway": "VLA-Stem addresses VLA policies that are trained for static manipulation and therefore lack handling of spatial constraints and dynamic obstacles, proposing a lightweight reinforcement-learning safety layer that leaves the underlying VLA policy unfrozen from fine-tuning. The method converts the VLA's action chunks into motion references and trains a Stem policy with teacher-student distillation and curriculum learning; conditioned on these references, proprioception, and local obstacle information, it adjusts execution at inference time. The abstract reports 52.8% average collision-free task success across six constrained simulation settings versus 23.7% for the strongest safety baseline, with preserved base-policy performance in obstacle-free settings and consistent collision reductions in real-world experiments. Inspect how action chunks are converted into references and how much timing flexibility the Stem policy retains.",
